  "body": "Part of #637 (step E2a; design in https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/637#issuecomment-6787218007, section 3 route (ii)).\n\nThe field's lattice is origin-locked (`cell_of(v) = floor(v / cell)`), and a `LatticeTurn`'s signed permutation maps cell `i` to cell `i` or `-i-1` exactly - cell centres onto cell centres. So a carried field can be re-indexed, never re-sampled, the way `Body::carry` re-indexes the column lattice: `SdfField::turned(&self, turn: &LatticeTurn) -> (SdfField, Point3)` returns the field with the turn's rotation/flip baked into its bricks and the turn's translation as the residual view offset.\n\nWhat the bake moves:\n- `bricks`, `cuts`: brick key `(b, slot) -> (-b-1, mirrored slot)` on a negated axis, keys swapped on a quarter turn;\n- on a flip, every `cut_ups` record becomes a `cut_downs` record (a new map on the field: \"the ray's entry going DOWN from the centre\"), and vice versa - the swap IS the record, nothing is recomputed;\n- `mesh` facets and `analytic` box transformed exactly; `cost` ledger rebuilt (`region_of`), dirty tracking reset.\n\nDone means: `turned` exists with `cut_downs` on the field; through all 8 turns, `turned(t).0.distance(p - shift) == CarriedField::new(f, t).distance(p)` bit-identical (or within 1 ulp, stated) for a cut block, cut layers included; a pinning test in `crates/sim/tests/field_carry.rs` or a new `field_turned.rs`; no shipped verdict changes (`stock_backend_parity`, `stock_engine_agreement` untouched). Nothing reads `cut_downs` yet (E2b).\n\nLabels wanted: P2, effort:high, area:sim, enhancement, source:agent.\n",
